# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command vectors
usage 1   vectors                       where each interrupt vector points, resolved through labels

case the fake target's table
target fake
covers 1
$ vectors
out 75
  RESET        $00FFFC -> $008000
native:
  NMI          $00FFEA -> $008009
status 0
action none
$ label add 8000 reset_handler
out 31
$008000 is now 'reset_handler'.
status 0
action none
$ vectors
out 91
  RESET        $00FFFC -> $008000 <reset_handler>
native:
  NMI          $00FFEA -> $008009
status 0
action none
$ cov on
out 22
Coverage recording on.
status 0
action none
$ vectors
out 91
  RESET        $00FFFC -> $008000 <reset_handler>
native:
  NMI          $00FFEA -> $008009
status 0
action none
end

case a bare target
target bare
covers 1
$ vectors
out 49
GOLDEN does not report an interrupt vector table.
status 0
action none
end

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ vectors
out 58
No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
end

case on venus
target venus
covers 1
$ vectors
out 370
Native (E=0):
  COP          $00FFE4 -> $00EAEA
  BRK          $00FFE6 -> $00EAEA
  ABORT        $00FFE8 -> $00EAEA
  NMI          $00FFEA -> $00EAEA
  IRQ          $00FFEE -> $00EAEA
Emulation (E=1):
  COP          $00FFF4 -> $00EAEA
  ABORT        $00FFF8 -> $00EAEA
  NMI          $00FFFA -> $00EAEA
  RESET        $00FFFC -> $008000
  IRQ/BRK      $00FFFE -> $00EAEA
status 0
action none
end

